# /model dialog: navigate, select a different model, confirm the applied
# result (internal/tui/dialog_model.go). Esc-to-cancel is covered
# separately in model-picker-esc.steps.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/dialogs-model.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE first task please
KEY enter
WAITFOR /you[\s\S]*kiln/ 20
SHOT turn-one
TYPE second task please
KEY enter
WAITFOR /you[\s\S]*kiln/ 20
SHOT turn-two
EXPECT /Second task done as well/
TYPE /model
WAIT 1
SHOT model-autocomplete
# design: Terminal.dc.html:220 (CMDS entry "/model" desc:'Switch model') —
# kiln's actual popup description is "Show or change the active model"
# (internal/commands/builtins.go modelCommand.Description), a real
# discrepancy from the design copy; asserting the design text here is
# expected to fail against the real binary.
EXPECT /Switch model/
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Select model/ 20
SHOT model-dialog-open
EXPECT /Select model/
EXPECT /Switch between models\. Your pick becomes the default for new sessions\. For other names, specify with --model\./
EXPECT /1\. faux\/faux-1[\s\S]*2\. faux\/faux-2/
EXPECT /Medium effort ←\/→ to adjust/
KEY down
SHOT model-dialog-selected
# Actual confirmation text (dialog_model.go) is "Model: faux/faux-2 ·
# small tier · 32.8k usable", not the "now on <model> — <tier> tier"
# wording this scenario originally assumed.
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Model: faux\/faux-2/ 20
SHOT model-dialog-applied
EXPECT /Model: faux\/faux-2 · small tier/
KEY esc
SHOT model-dialog-closed
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
